  "scientific_limitations": [
    "Optimizing unweighted L2 on z=(temperature-baseline)/profile_scale is equivalent to weighting Celsius squared error by profile_scale^-2; rows with smaller profile scale receive greater effective Celsius-MSE weight.",
    "v1r2 records this weighting consequence but deliberately does not add sample weights or alter the preregistered model mathematics."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Filesystem hashing and Python import cannot be one operating-system-atomic transaction; the sealed bundle is checked before import, after import, before every fit reservation, after every fit, and before publish.",
    "A hard crash can leave the permanent claim, an incomplete durable journal, or hidden staging; all such states are intentionally reported and fail closed with no automatic rerun.",
    "Directory fsync is best effort on Windows; every claim, journal append, result, and manifest file itself is flushed with os.fsync, and final publication uses same-filesystem directory rename.",
    "The 1800-second hard wall covers worker preprocessing, all physical fits, predictions, and local metric construction; parent-side terminal journal append and atomic final publication can occur after a successfully returned worker but cannot start another fit.",
    "The repository may be dirty because pre-existing user work is preserved; Git HEAD and dirty state are recorded, while every experiment-relevant implementation and lineage file is independently hash-pinned."
  ]
